{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1790874900000-architect-python-c2-generators-design.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '119,180p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1036,1066p'; rg -n 'iter-at|iterable' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '502,523p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba collab/1790874900000-architect-python-c2-generators-design.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md | sed -n '119,180p'; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc | sed -n '1036,1066p'; rg -n 'iter-at|iterable' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; nl -ba src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc | sed -n '502,523p'\"","aggregated_output":"   119\t\n   120\t- **Tracing.** Already sufficient; no VM change. Cell content is traced as data, and a `Continuation` re-enters kernel mode through its payload (`engine.cljc:1948-1949`). The walker classifies it precisely (`ast_walker.cljc:1153`); the semantic kernel answers nil, so the payload is walked whole, which is conservative and complete (`semantic.cljc:1058`). C1 already keeps handler continuations in a cell, so the path is exercised.\n   121\t- **Dropped mid-suspension.** The cell is swept with its continuation. Pending `finally` and `__exit__` do not run. This conforms to the language reference and matches §8.11 (finalizers out of scope). Close-on-collection stays deferred.\n   122\t- **Pinning.** No new rule. A generator ref put on a stream is pinned for the task's life with everything its continuation reaches.\n   123\t- **Stale base (design limit).** `%capture` is undelimited, so `:resume` contains the frames of the first `next()` call beneath the generator's own. They are never returned into, but they are traced, so the first caller's locals stay live until the generator closes or is swept. The principled fix is a VM-level delimited capture, which is outside C2.\n   124\t- **Allocation.** Two flag cells per item (one per crossing), garbage after re-entry.\n   125\t\n   126\t## Q6. Identity and wire\n   127\t\n   128\t- **Canonical tree.** Unchanged. `yield` is an `:application` of `py/yield`; `%capture` stays inside prelude functions.\n   129\t- **Ledger.** No new record. \"Is this function a generator\" is derivable by query (its body applies `py/yield` to its `%gen` binder), so nothing is persisted.\n   130\t- **Code addresses.** The prelude grows, so every bundled unit's address changes; this is a prelude-profile bump under §11.\n   131\t- **UCF.** No change. A reachable generator is non-portable today for two existing reasons: cells refuse (slice 1) and continuations refuse as `:non-canonicalizable` (`engine.cljc:710-712`). When heap-slice lift and the `:yin.k/frame` continuation encoding land, generators migrate with no generator-specific wire form, stale base included.\n   132\t- **Guest identity.** `is` is `=` on the ref; `iter(g) is g`; hashable by ref. `py/snapshot-obj` gains `{:py/generator name}`, never the continuation.\n   133\t- **Prelude rule.** Compare only `:state` keywords, never generator contents: `Continuation` equality and hash are structural and cost O(continuation).\n   134\t\n   135\t## Q7. Portability\n   136\t\n   137\t- **Hosts.** All new code is prelude Universal AST and portable lowering. No host type, no reader conditional. No `get` on a continuation (the flag cell avoids it).\n   138\t- **Tail marks.** A crossing is abortive in both directions, so neither side grows. The generator's loop and `py/yield-from`'s recursion are tail calls that `mark-tails` marks. The walker reuses `k` on closure application (`ast_walker.cljc:266-271`); semantic, stack and register honour the mark. Continuation size is the constant body frames plus the fixed stale base.\n   139\t- **`sys.settrace`.** Sees nothing in C2. The obligation to the safepoint design is that generator switches happen only at applications of `py/gen-switch`, `py/yield-raw` and `py/yield-from`, which an attached inserter can find by query.\n   140\t- **Forward constraint.** Future per-thread dynamic state (frame-record stack, recursion counter, `exc_info`) must join `:ctx` and swap with the handler stack.\n   141\t\n   142\t## Q8. Slices and acceptance contracts\n   143\t\n   144\t**Lanes.**\n   145\t- **JVM:** e2e from source on all four VMs via `every-vm=`; expected output is CPython 3.9.6's for the same source.\n   146\t- **Node:** the same primitives as prelude-notation forms in `prelude_parity_test.cljc`, and hand-built packets in `lower_portable_test.cljc`.\n   147\t- **Dart:** the prelude forms wherever the parity lane runs on CLJD.\n   148\t\n   149\t**S1: core.** `py/make-generator`, `gen-switch`, `yield`, `gen-exit`, `gen-fail`; `StopIteration`; `next`; `iter-at`/`iterable` arms; lowering arms `yield_stmt` and `yield_expr`, a `:gen` binder in ctx reset in every nested scope, and removal of the three `yield` guards.\n   150\t\n   151\t| Setup | Action | Assertion |\n   152\t|---|---|---|\n   153\t| `def g(n)` yielding `0..n-1` in a `while` | `print(list(g(3)))`; `for x in g(2): print(x)` | `[0, 1, 2]`, `0`, `1` |\n   154\t| body appends `'start'`, yields 1, appends `'end'` | call; `next`; `next` under `except StopIteration as e` | log empty after call; `1 ['start']`; `stop None ['start', 'end']` |\n   155\t| `yield 1; return 7` | drain with `next` | `e.value` is 7; a further `next` gives value None |\n   156\t| `x = [a(), (yield 1), b()]` with logging `a`, `b` | `next`, then `send('s')` | `a` logged before suspension, `b` after; list holds `'s'` |\n   157\t| `yield` at module level; `[(yield x) for x in y]` | compile | one `:yang.python.antlr/syntax` diagnostic, no program |\n   158\t| generator yielding in `while True` | consume 3000 items in a `for` with `break` | completes on all four VMs; JVM-only: continuation length of `:resume` equal after 10 and after 1000 items |\n   159\t| Node: prelude form building a generator from a literal body | `py/gen-switch` three times | `[:yield 1]`, `[:yield 2]`, `[:return :py/None]` on every VM |\n   160\t\n   161\t**S2: send, throw, close, dynamic context.**\n   162\t\n   163\t| Setup | Action | Assertion |\n   164\t|---|---|---|\n   165\t| accumulator `x = yield total` | `next(a), a.send(5), a.send(2)` | `0 5 7` |\n   166\t| fresh generator | `send(1)` | `TypeError`; generator still startable |\n   167\t| `try: yield 1 / except ValueError: yield 'caught'` | `next`; `throw(ValueError)` | `'caught'` |\n   168\t| no handler in body | `throw(KeyError('k'))`; `next` | `KeyError` at caller; then `StopIteration` |\n   169\t| `try: yield 1 / finally: log` | `close()` twice | finally logged once; both return None |\n   170\t| `try: yield / except GeneratorExit: yield 2` | `close()` | `RuntimeError` \"generator ignored GeneratorExit\" |\n   171\t| `with cm: yield 1` | `close()` | `__exit__` called once with the `GeneratorExit` type |\n   172\t| body `try: yield 1; yield 2 / finally: log`, then `raise KeyError` | first `next` inside a caller `try/except ValueError`, later ones outside | `1`, `2`, then `KeyError` caught by the current caller's handler; a later caller `try/except` still works |\n   173\t| body calls `next` on itself | `next` | `ValueError` \"generator already executing\" |\n   174\t| body raises `StopIteration` | `next` | `RuntimeError` |\n   175\t| consumer `for` with `break` over a generator with `finally` | run, then raise and catch in caller | finally not logged; caller handler works |\n   176\t\n   177\t**S3: `yield from`, `iter`, sequence iterators.**\n   178\t\n   179\t| Setup | Action | Assertion |\n   180\t|---|---|---|\n  1036\t(defn- lower-funcdef\n  1037\t  [ctx n]\n  1038\t  (let [ks (kids ctx n)\n  1039\t        nm (name-of ctx (first (rules ctx n \"name\")))\n  1040\t        params (first (rules ctx n \"parameters\"))]\n  1041\t    (when (some #(p/token? % \"->\") ks) (unsupported! n \"return annotation\"))\n  1042\t    (assign-name\n  1043\t      ctx nm\n  1044\t      (function-value\n  1045\t        ctx n nm\n  1046\t        (param-spec ctx (first (rules ctx params \"typedargslist\")) \"tfpdef\")\n  1047\t        (fn [fctx]\n  1048\t          (let [block (first (rules ctx n \"block\"))]\n  1049\t            (if (contains-rule? ctx block \"return_stmt